#
# Failing control for math:TensorAxisExtentChoiceConstraint: the one axis of a rank-1
# shape declares both a concrete extent and a symbolic extent. Each is well formed on
# its own (4 is zero or greater; the symbolic extent names a free-variable declaration
# with a typed domain) and the shape is otherwise consistent; claiming both is the
# only defect. Bound by ex:ecTensorAxisExtentBoth.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/tensor-shape-controls/> .

ex:shape a math:TensorShape ; math:tensorRank 1 ; math:shapeAxis ex:axis .
ex:axis a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 ;
    math:axisExtent 4 ; math:symbolicExtent ex:batch .
ex:batch a math:FreeVariableDeclaration ; math:variableDomain math:naturalNumbers .
